  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result so far is config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) at 0.5266 acc, showing a clear ~4% gain over RNA-only (config_001, 0.4849). However, we have only tested singleprofile; the multiprofile setting remains entirely unexplored. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) on top of the best-known multimodal setup further improve accuracy? config_018 is the minimal, single-axis extension of config_016 (changing only profile_setting from single→multi and adding avgpool aggregation), isolating the effect of multiprofile aggregation while keeping the proven RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy fixed. This is the highest-information experiment under the remaining 6-slot budget because multiprofile is a major untested design axis that could yield substantial gains or reveal diminishing returns, directly guiding whether to invest further experiments in aggregation strategies (transformer) or pivot to alternative encoders."
}

